{"w":2400,"h":3395,"lines":[{"y":0.046511627815782663,"w":0.069958845774332645,"c":0.30000001192092896,"h":0.008720930389296444,"x":0.77160493914987061,"t":"1718867188"},{"c":1,"x":0.10288065676349907,"t":"READING PASSAGE 3","w":0.28806584676106772,"y":0.12499999986411847,"h":0.014575971731448756},{"y":0.15842167235748272,"c":1,"x":0.10288066774334065,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading","w":0.77160491943359366,"h":0.017450420819968837},{"t":"Passage 3 below.","x":0.10050435770497344,"y":0.17420861506611496,"w":0.16122047424316405,"h":0.017742029488858946,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.69353139241536454,"t":"Building the Skyline: The Birth and Growth of Manhattan's","x":0.14603343296813609,"y":0.21071100912997787,"h":0.020806300204830874},{"x":0.42096930887544298,"t":"Skyscrapers","y":0.23515588143627963,"h":0.021998635731260152,"c":1,"w":0.14338549296061204},{"c":1,"y":0.27325581379427244,"t":"Katharine L. Shester reviews a book by Jason Barr about the development of","w":0.72633743286132824,"x":0.13168725054493688,"h":0.017441860778592999},{"y":0.29313930678675026,"t":"New York City","h":0.018372549185062148,"w":0.13808994293212895,"c":1,"x":0.42375338232990278},{"y":0.32703488357480126,"t":"In Building the Skyline, Jason Barr takes the reader through a detailed history of New York","x":0.10082304485001098,"w":0.72427983601888024,"h":0.016015764400450716,"c":1},{"y":0.34447674404010509,"c":1,"x":0.10082303919428426,"w":0.76131688435872391,"h":0.01598837238037687,"t":"City. The book combines geology, history, economics, and a lot of data to explain why business"},{"x":0.10082305306038933,"y":0.36042402838168819,"c":1,"h":0.016029460129664885,"w":0.72633743286132812,"t":"clusters developed where they did and how the early decisions of workers and firms shaped"},{"t":"the skyline we see today. Building the Skyline is organized into two distinct parts. The first is","x":0.098722281260157654,"y":0.37641400665333935,"c":1,"w":0.74083257039388017,"h":0.017340774109282031},{"h":0.015998644317698707,"y":0.39389534869106524,"x":0.10082303481037105,"c":1,"t":"primarily historical and addresses New York's settlement and growth from 1609 to 1900; the","w":0.73456792195638021},{"w":0.72016459147135414,"h":0.015988371257085521,"c":1,"y":0.40988372118831773,"t":"second deals primarily with the 20th century and is a compilation of chapters commenting","x":0.10082306064292358},{"c":1,"t":"on different aspects of New York's urban development. The tone and organization of the book","x":0.10082305019162628,"y":0.42726737343060539,"w":0.74485595703124996,"h":0.014723203769140047},{"y":0.44316843321361299,"x":0.10288064956738736,"t":"changes somewhat between the first and second parts, as the latter chapters incorporate aspects of","w":0.77983540852864586,"h":0.014723203769140158,"c":1},{"t":"Barr's related research papers.","h":0.016608027041449813,"c":1,"y":0.45921414159360074,"w":0.24527056376139325,"x":0.10062446370618436},{"x":0.10082305778744285,"y":0.49116607756409725,"t":"Barr begins chapter one by taking the reader on a 'helicopter time-machine' ride - giving a","w":0.72633743286132812,"h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1},{"t":"fascinating account of how the New York landscape in 1609 might have looked from the sky. He","y":0.51017441847206113,"c":1,"w":0.76954732259114578,"x":0.098765433250633902,"h":0.014560564106288587},{"c":1,"t":"then moves on to a subterranean walking tour of the city, indicating the location of rock and water","x":0.098765439520928269,"y":0.52616279054412829,"w":0.78395060221354163,"h":0.01598837238037687},{"y":0.54358068336355692,"c":1,"w":0.77983540852864586,"t":"below the subsoil, before taking the reader back to the surface. His love of the city comes through","h":0.014558851648696969,"x":0.10082303638179117},{"w":0.77366256713867188,"c":1,"t":"as he describes various fun facts about the location of the New York residence of early 19th-century","x":0.10082303730597024,"h":0.016195524146054185,"y":0.55948174313344345},{"h":0.017450420258323218,"c":1,"w":0.57818929036458322,"t":"vice-president Aaron Burr as well as a number of legends about the city.","x":0.10082305541441604,"y":0.57412790720723295},{"h":0.016048292108362783,"x":0.10082305487044815,"w":0.71399175008138016,"t":"Chapters two and three take the reader up to the Civil War (1861-1865), with chapter two","y":0.60895170803238585,"c":1},{"t":"focusing on the early development of land and the implementation of a grid system in 1811.","y":0.62632508818042554,"w":0.73868311564127598,"h":0.014723203769140158,"c":1,"x":0.098765437960089172},{"y":0.64244186033240058,"h":0.01453488398216074,"x":0.10082304013608459,"t":"Chapter three focuses on land use before the Civil War. Both chapters are informative and well","w":0.75514404296874993,"c":1},{"t":"researched and set the stage for the economic analysis that comes later in the book. I would","y":0.65796538263141879,"x":0.10077401289250114,"w":0.72851379394531257,"h":0.016170671887616783,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.67432273254942576,"x":0.10082305694896547,"t":"have liked Barr to expand upon his claim that existing tenements* prevented skyscrapers in","w":0.72633743286132812,"h":0.014723203769140158},{"h":0.016031172025610885,"t":"certain neighborhoods because 'likely no skyscraper developer was interested in performing the","c":1,"w":0.76543207804361979,"y":0.69186046496936582,"x":0.10082305548927782},{"h":0.017441860778592999,"w":0.77572016398111976,"y":0.70784883704996859,"c":1,"x":0.10082304549051742,"t":"necessary \"slum clearance\"'. Later in the book, Barr makes the claim that the depth of bedrock**"},{"y":0.72526501741700367,"w":0.7592592366536457,"t":"was not a limiting factor for developers, as foundation costs were a small fraction of the cost of","c":1,"h":0.014560564106288587,"x":0.10288066967282901},{"x":0.10082305457590603,"w":0.77160491943359377,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1,"t":"development. At first glance, it is not obvious why slum clearance would be limiting, while more","y":0.74263839810006449},{"x":0.10288065959888361,"t":"expensive foundations would not.","w":0.26954732259114583,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"y":0.75872093010730945},{"t":"* a tenement: a multi-occupancy building of any sort, but particularly a run-down apartment building or slum building","w":0.64814814249674479,"c":1,"y":0.83274440528540306,"x":0.10699588749380259,"h":0.010306242638398078},{"t":"** bedrock: the solid, hard rock in the ground that lies under a loose layer of soil","y":0.84589614523356838,"x":0.1007600958020276,"w":0.44867090861002612,"h":0.012446660737126414,"c":1},{"w":0.024691357612609877,"t":"67","h":0.013081395583944722,"x":0.8580246914705375,"y":0.86773255796252025,"c":1},{"t":"IELTSXpress.com","x":0.66991655033568553,"y":0.95314993796778535,"c":1,"h":0.03375352650564889,"w":0.30612678527832038}]}